whpx: continue when the host refuses nested virtualization

Applies on top of cmspam/winq-emu-qemu commit 2ce303cf (QEMU 11.0.0 base).

whpx_accel_init() asks WHP for nested virtualization whenever the kernel
irqchip is in use and the processor feature banks advertise
NestedVirtSupport. Some hosts advertise it and then refuse the partition
property with hr=0x80370302: Intel Core Ultra (Meteor Lake) laptops on
Windows 11 23H2 and machines running the full Hyper-V feature set. The old
code treated that as fatal, so Try Omarchy could not start at all on those
machines (issue #19). The guest never needs nested virtualization, so log a
warning and keep going with the kernel irqchip intact. Chainfire's binary
patch for QEMU 11.0.0 defuses the same branch.

diff --git a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
index a437421..246755c 100644
--- a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
+++ b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
@@ -2322,10 +2322,16 @@ int whpx_accel_init(AccelState *as, MachineState *ms)
             WHvPartitionPropertyCodeNestedVirtualization,
             &prop,
             sizeof(WHV_PARTITION_PROPERTY));
-            if (FAILED(hr)) {
-                error_report("WHPX: Failed to enable nested virtualization, hr=%08lx", hr);
-                ret = -EINVAL;
-                goto error;
+        if (FAILED(hr)) {
+            /*
+             * Some hosts advertise NestedVirtSupport but refuse to delegate
+             * it to a WHP partition (hr=0x80370302 on Meteor Lake laptops
+             * and on machines running the full Hyper-V feature set). The
+             * guest never needs nested virtualization, so keep the kernel
+             * irqchip and carry on without it instead of failing to start.
+             */
+            warn_report("WHPX: nested virtualization unavailable (hr=%08lx), "
+                        "continuing without it", hr);
         }
     }
 
